    <string name="l_viisarit_title">Two hands</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_desc">What does each hand show?</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_p1a">This clock has two hands.</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_p1b">The short pink hand is the hour hand. It shows which hour we are in.</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_p2a">The long blue hand is the minute hand. It shows the minutes.</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_p3a">As time passes, the hands move from 1 towards 2, then 3, and on around the clock.</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_p3b">We call this direction clockwise.</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_q">Which hand shows the hour?</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_c1">The short pink hand</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_c2">The long blue hand</string>
    <string name="l_viisarit_hint">The hour hand is the shorter, pink hand.</string>

    <string name="l_kierros_title">One trip around</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_desc">What happens in one hour?</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_p1a">The long hand keeps moving around the clock.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_p1b">One whole trip around takes one hour.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_say_start">It is three o\'clock.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_say_go">The long hand starts its trip.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_say_end">Now it is four o\'clock. One hour has passed!</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_p2a">Now watch the short hand!</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_p2b">While the long hand goes all the way around, the short hand moves forward just one number.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_say_moved">The short hand moved from 3 to 4.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_p3a">One hour has 60\u00A0minutes.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_p3b">There are 60\u00A0minute marks around the edge. The long hand moves from one mark to the next each minute.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_say_hour">60\u00A0minutes make one hour.</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_q">How much time passes when the long hand goes all the way around?</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_c1">One hour</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_c2">One minute</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_c3">One day</string>
    <string name="l_kierros_hint">The short hand moved forward one number. That is one hour.</string>

    <string name="l_tasan_title">Whole hours</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_desc">The long hand points straight up</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_p1a">When the long hand points straight up at 12, it is a whole hour.</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_p2a">Look at the short hand to find the hour.</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_p2b">Here it points at 3, so it is three o\'clock.</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_p3a">Let\'s explore some other whole hours.</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_p3b">The long hand stays at the top. The short hand tells us the hour.</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_q">What time is it?</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_c1">Nine o\'clock</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_c2">Twelve o\'clock</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_c3">Three o\'clock</string>
    <string name="l_tasan_hint">The long hand is at the top. Look at the short pink hand for the hour.</string>

    <string name="l_puoli_title">Half past</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_desc">The long hand points down</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p1a">After half a trip around the clock, the long hand points down at 6.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p1b">Half an hour has passed. That is 30\u00A0minutes.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_say_half">Half an hour has passed.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p2a">The short hand has left 3 but has not reached 4 yet.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p2b">It is halfway between them.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p3a">We say half past three: half an hour has passed since three o\'clock.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p3b">In numbers, it is 3:30.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_say_digits">Half past three is 3:30.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p4a">After half past, name the hour the short hand has passed.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_p4b">Between 7 and 8, it is half past seven.</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_q">What time is it?</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_c1">Half past five</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_c2">Half past four</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_c3">Six o\'clock</string>
    <string name="l_puoli_hint">The short hand has passed 5 and is halfway to 6. Name the hour it has passed.</string>

    <string name="l_vartti_title">Quarter hours</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_desc">A quarter of an hour</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_p1a">Divide one hour into four equal parts. Each part is a quarter of an hour.</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_p1b">A quarter of an hour is 15\u00A0minutes.</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_say_four">Four quarters make one hour.</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_p2a">When the long hand reaches 3, a quarter of the hour has passed.</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_p2b">Here we say quarter past three.</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_p3a">When the long hand reaches 9, there is a quarter of an hour left until the next whole hour.</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_p3b">Here we say quarter to four.</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_q">What time is it?</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_c1">Quarter to seven</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_c2">Quarter past six</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_c3">Quarter to six</string>
    <string name="l_vartti_hint">The long hand is at 9. There is a quarter of an hour left. Which hour comes next?</string>

    <string name="l_ylivaille_title">Past and to</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_desc">Two sides of the clock</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_p1a">On the right side, we can say past.</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_p1b">We count how many minutes have passed since the whole hour.</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_p2a">On the left side, we can say to.</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_p2b">We count how many minutes remain until the next whole hour.</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_p3a">With past, name the hour the short hand has passed.</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_p3b">With to, name the hour that comes next.</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_q">What time is it?</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_c1">Ten past four</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_c2">Ten to four</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_c3">Ten to five</string>
    <string name="l_ylivaille_hint">The long hand is on the right. Count past the hour the short hand has passed.</string>

    <string name="l_viisi_title">Five-minute steps</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_desc">Numbers and minutes</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_p1a">For the long hand, each step from one number to the next takes five minutes.</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_p1b">Number 1 marks 5\u00A0minutes, number 2 marks 10, and so on.</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_p2a">Count in fives: 5, 10, 15, 20.</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_p2b">At number 4, 20\u00A0minutes have passed. We say twenty past.</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_p3a">Keep counting in fives on either side of half past.</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_p3b">At number 5, say twenty-five past. At number 7, say twenty-five to the next hour.</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_q">What time is it?</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_c1">Twenty to nine</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_c2">Twenty past eight</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_c3">Ten to nine</string>
    <string name="l_viisi_hint">At number 8, 40\u00A0minutes have passed. There are 20\u00A0minutes left until the next hour.</string>

    <string name="l_minuutit_title">Exact minutes</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_desc">The small marks</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_p1a">Each small mark around the clock represents one minute.</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_p1b">There are 5\u00A0minutes between neighbouring numbers.</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_p2a">Start at the numbered mark just before the long hand. Count the extra small marks forward.</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_p2b">Number 2 marks 10\u00A0minutes. Two more marks make 10 + 2 = 12\u00A0minutes.</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_q">What time is it?</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_c1">Seven minutes past three</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_c2">Five past three</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_c3">Eight minutes past three</string>
    <string name="l_minuutit_hint">Number 1 marks 5\u00A0minutes. Count two more small marks forward.</string>

    <string name="l_vrk_title">24\u00A0hours in a day</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_desc">Morning, afternoon, and night</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_p1a">One whole day has 24\u00A0hours.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_p1b">The short hand goes around the clock twice each day.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_say_first">First trip: midnight to noon</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_say_second">Second trip: noon to midnight</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_say_day">One whole day has passed.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_p2a">For afternoon and evening hours from 1 to 11, add 12 to get the 24-hour number.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_p2b">Three in the afternoon is 3 + 12 = 15. We write 15:00.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_say_night">Three at night: 03:00</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_say_sum">3 + 12 = 15: the time is 15:00.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_p3a">The hands look the same at three at night and three in the afternoon.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_p3b">Read the label under the clock to find the part of the day. The hands alone cannot tell you.</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_say_afternoon">Three in the afternoon: 15:00</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_q">What time is it?</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_c1">Seven in the evening: 19:00</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_c2">Seven in the morning: 07:00</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_c3">Five in the afternoon: 17:00</string>
    <string name="l_vrk_hint">The label under the clock says evening. Add 12 to the hour: 7 + 12 = 19.</string>
